# CHAIN-LINK corpus · AXIS = which RETURN-TYPE ladder arm publishes the outer
# link's type. CELL SAMPLED HERE: the SET half of the same bool-predicate arm
# `chain_link_bool_builtin` samples on the String half
# (`is_subset` / `is_empty` / `contains` over a `Set`).
#
# One `if method_name == "is_empty" or … or "is_subset" or …` arm in
# `infer_expr_type` serves BOTH receivers, so a per-arm publish would have fixed
# or broken them together — but the two receivers reach the arm through
# different resolution paths, and "one arm, therefore one behaviour" is exactly
# the kind of reasoning Core #12 says to measure instead of assert. Measured:
# RED pre-fix, `incompatible types when assigning to type 'GorgetSet' from type
# '_Bool'`, and green after.
#
# The `is_subset` row also samples the arm with an ARGUMENT, which the String
# rows do not: the receiver and the argument are both chains-worth of spine, and
# only the receiver's spine can contend for `span.start`.
struct Holder:
    Set[int] s

equip Holder:
    Set[int] grab(self):
        return self.s

void main():
    Set[int] a = Set[int]()
    a.add(1)
    a.add(2)
    Set[int] b = Set[int]()
    b.add(1)
    Holder h = Holder(b)
    print(h.grab().is_subset(a))
    print(h.grab().is_empty())
    print(h.grab().contains(1))
